<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mellifont Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1142</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mellifont Abbey, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-louth">County Louth</a>, was the first Cistercian monastery in Ireland, founded in 1142 by Saint Malachy with monks from Clairvaux, under the patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnchad-ua-cerbaill">Donnchad Ua Cerbaill</a>, king of Airgialla. It became the mother house of many Irish Cistercian abbeys. It was dissolved in 1539, and the Treaty of Mellifont ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> was signed there in 1603.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mellifont-abbey.jpg" alt="Mellifont Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brholden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mellifont_Abbey_lavabo_County_Louth_Ireland.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
